# Baseline run side effects: logs, checkpoints, per-step traces.
runs/

# Unpublished methods stay out of git entirely. Ignoring them here is
# what makes them unpublishable: code that cannot be committed cannot
# be pushed.
#
# Tracking them was tried and reverted. A push publishes whole trees,
# not diffs, so once one of these files is committed, every descendant
# commit carries it and the only remedy is rewriting history -- after
# which the objects still sit on the remote, reachable by hash.
#
# The pre-push hook is a second line of defence, not the first. It
# lives in .git/hooks/pre-push and is not tracked, because naming the
# method in a tracked file is the thing being prevented. It inspects
# only the pushed tip, so it does not catch a name left behind in an
# older commit -- that gap is why ignoring has to do the real work. A
# fresh clone gets neither the hook nor these files; install the hook
# before adding a remote.
#
# Results stay out too: artefact paths carry the algorithm's name, and
# nothing about a run needs to be in git.
topogym/baselines/**/concrete_baselines/_private_*.py
tests/baselines/**/test_private_*.py
scripts/benchmarks/_private_*.py
benchmarks/**/private/
# EpicChase is the standalone certificate family: its whole tree is
# committed locally (never pushed until the method is published); the
# private/ split inside it only exists because the runner writes there.
!benchmarks/epicchase/private/
!benchmarks/epicchase/private/**
# EnlargedChamberCount is the same family with the door separation
# guaranteed instead of incidental, and gets the same treatment for
# the same reason: the arms under private/ are the comparison, so a
# tree committed without them records only the control.
!benchmarks/ecc/private/
!benchmarks/ecc/private/**
# OpenFieldChamberCount is the third of the same lineage -- the same
# guarantee with the boundary moved out of reach -- and its arms live
# under private/ for the same reason.
!benchmarks/ofcc/private/
!benchmarks/ofcc/private/**
benchmarks/private/
runs/**/private/
runs/private/
